  "notes": "Whole principal Hongu sanctuary ensemble: all16 vertices of main building57008547, both separate6-point inner gate roofs57008548/57008551 and whole24-point outer worship hall373238591. Preserve the main building, flanking low sections and south spur, two inner roofed gates and full outer hall/wings with open passages. Original four wood-palisade traces remain thin intrinsic architectural fences with their native gaps. Steep copper-gray Shinmei gables, exposed wood posts/boards/brackets, projecting ridge ends, forked chigi and cylindrical gold-ended katsuogi. Exclude the separate Kagura-den, Doyoden, treasure hall, other shrines, whole wooded religious parcel, natural ground/trees/people/flags/signs/crest art/sacred interiors."
